# AI test generator — execution model

## Cursor Agent CLI (headless)

- Run **only** inside **GitHub Actions** (the workflow that installs the CLI and invokes it).
- **Do not** add npm scripts, Makefile targets, or docs that tell people to run `cursor-agent` / `agent` on a laptop or CI other than that workflow.
- **Do not** commit automation that shells out to the headless agent locally.

## Local development (Cursor IDE)

- Use **Cursor IDE** with this repository: **rules**, **`.cursor/skills/`**, **`.cursor/mcp.json`** (from **`.cursor/mcp.template.json`** via **`render-mcp-config.js`** or filled locally — gitignored), and Jira MCP.
- You may hand-author or edit files under **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`** (the story key, not the Sub-task dispatch key when they differ); the **headless** generation step is CI-only.

## Jira story test methodology (skill)

- For **how** to derive manual tests from a Jira story (AC, Gherkin, scope, GA judgment, splitting cases, naming), follow **`.cursor/skills/jira-story-test-cases-md/SKILL.md`**.
- In **GitHub Actions**, the skill’s **Headless CI** section **overrides** the Markdown deliverable — see that section when `CI=true`.

## GitHub Actions — non-interactive

- **Never** ask the user any blocking question. CI has no human in the loop.
- Apply **Path A (default RPP)** style logic; if **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`** is absent, use the skill’s **Authoring rules** + **Markdown document shape** as the *logical* style, while still emitting **`tests.json`** per below.

## CI — Sub-task dispatch: requirements **only** from the story

When **`ISSUE_KEY`** is a **Sub-task** and **`STORY_KEY`** is its **parent**, **all** material for test design comes **only** from **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`**: the story’s **Description**, **summary** (title context), **`issuetype`**, **`parent`**, and any **Acceptance Criteria / DoD** custom fields the MCP returns for **that** issue. **Do not** use **`jira_getIssue(ISSUE_KEY)`** (Sub-task) **description** or **summary** to define tests. If the story body is empty, do not substitute Sub-task text—note the gap instead.

## Output directory

Write **only** under **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`**, where **`<STORY_KEY>`** is the issue you used as the **story source** for tests. In CI, **`STORY_KEY`** is pre-resolved from the workflow target: if the target is a **Sub-task**, it is the **parent** issue key; otherwise it matches the target. **`<STORY_KEY>`** is also where new **Test** issues should link (the story).

## Manifest schema (`tests.json`) — canonical

Path: **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/tests.json`** (see **Output directory** for **`STORY_KEY`** vs Sub-task).

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "tests": [
    {
      "summary": "string (required)",
      "testSteps": "string (Preconditions + Steps as plain text for Jira Test Steps field)",
      "expectedResult": "string (maps to Expected result custom field)",
      "description": "optional Markdown"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **Project, issue type, and custom fields** for new Tests: **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-create.mdc`** (edit that rule for your Jira).
- **`summary` (Jira Test title):** Must include **`STORY_KEY`** as a substring (e.g. **`[EPMRPP-12345] Area. Page. Behavior`** or **`EPMRPP-12345 — Area. Page. Behavior`**). When the workflow target was a **Sub-task**, **do not** put the Sub-task key in **`summary`**—use **`STORY_KEY`** only. See **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`** (CI / **`tests.json`**).
- **Create and link every Test issue only via Jira MCP** (`@atlassian-dc-mcp/jira`). Use **`jira_createIssue`**, **`jira_updateIssue`**, and any linking approach your MCP tools support so each new Test is associated with the **story** (**`STORY_KEY`**).

## `meta.json` (required after MCP create)

After **every** Test exists in Jira and is linked to the parent, write **`meta.json`** next to **`tests.json`**:

```json
{
  "jiraPublish": "mcp",
  "mcpCreatedKeys": ["PROJ-201", "PROJ-202"]
}
```

- **`mcpCreatedKeys`**: same **length** and **order** as **`tests`** in `tests.json`.
- **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** runs in CI; the job **fails** if **`meta.json`** is missing or invalid, or if any **`tests[].summary`** does not contain **`STORY_KEY`**. There is **no** REST publish path for Test issues.

## Jira: MCP only (Test creation)

- **Read** requirements **only** from **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** (Description, summary for title context, AC/DoD custom fields). **Do not** use the Sub-task’s (**`ISSUE_KEY`**) description or summary for test design when it is not the story. Then **`jira_searchIssues`** / other reads only if they add context **about the same story**.
- **Write** (create/update Test issues, link to the story) **only** through MCP tools. Do not rely on repository scripts to create Jira issues.
- If your MCP server cannot link issues, use the same tooling stack your team uses with that server (still MCP-side); the pipeline does not run a REST publisher.

## Jira MCP in CI

- MCP config: rendered **`.cursor/mcp.json`** from **`.cursor/mcp.template.json`** on the runner.
- Prefer the **same Jira project** as the parent issue unless requirements say otherwise.

## Local MCP (`mcp.json`)

- Edit **`.cursor/mcp.template.json`** (uses **`@atlassian-dc-mcp/jira`**; placeholders **`JIRA_HOST`** / **`JIRA_API_TOKEN`**), then run **`node scripts/render-mcp-config.js`** with **`JIRA_API_TOKEN`** and either **`JIRA_HOST`** or **`JIRA_BASE_URL`** (host is derived from the URL), or copy the rendered output to **`.cursor/mcp.json`** manually.

## Safety

- **Never** write secrets or tokens into repo files under **`generated/`** or elsewhere.
